{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015sJdbhgm5W19pWJbyi6W9G","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd113-pee\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/pee: Tee Standard Input to Pipes\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  pee (from moreutils) reads stdin and writes it to multiple commands simultaneously,\n6\t  like tee but for pipe commands instead of files. The Go implementation must match the\n7\t  Homebrew reference binary (pee, installed by moreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by\n8\t  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Read stdin and pipe it to multiple commands simultaneously.\n12\t  - G2: Verify functional parity against the reference pee binary via differential testing.\n13\t\n14\trequirements:\n15\t  R1:\n16\t    title: Pipe teeing\n17\t    items:\n18\t      - R1.1:\n19\t          text: Must accept one or more COMMAND arguments. Must read stdin and write the input to the stdin of each COMMAND in parallel. Each COMMAND is executed via the shell (sh -c COMMAND).\n20\t      - R1.2:\n21\t          text: Must wait for all commands to complete before exiting.\n22\t      - R1.3:\n23\t          text: Stdout of each COMMAND goes to stdout, interleaved.\n24\t\n25\t  R2:\n26\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n27\t    items:\n28\t      - R2.1:\n29\t          text: Must exit 0 when all commands exit 0. Must exit 1 when any command exits non-zero.\n30\t      - R2.2:\n31\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n32\t\n33\tnon_goals:\n34\t  - cmd/pee does not implement output ordering or serialization of command outputs.\n35\t\n36\tacceptance_criteria:\n37\t  - id: AC1\n38\t    criterion: \"echo hello | pee 'cat' 'wc -c' writes hello and byte count, matching reference.\"\n39\t    traces:\n40\t      - R1.1\n41\t      - R1.3\n42\t  - id: AC2\n43\t    criterion: \"Differential test against reference pee passes.\"\n44\t    traces:\n45\t      - R1.1\n46\t  - id: AC3\n47\t    criterion: \"cmd/pee compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n48\t    traces:\n49\t      - R1.1\n50\t      - R1.2\n51\t      - R1.3\n52\t      - R2.1\n53\t      - R2.2\n54\t\n55\tpackage_contract:\n56\t  imports:\n57\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eda0914b-c5d5-43fb-b2bd-a6e814808fd4","uuid":"deef6e58-8468-4d4c-b7b8-24ad391889ad","timestamp":"2026-05-28T17:04:14.203Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5633/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd113-pee.yaml","content":"id: srd113-pee\ntitle: \"cmd/pee: Tee Standard Input to Pipes\"\n\nproblem: |\n  pee (from moreutils) reads stdin and writes it to multiple commands simultaneously,\n  like tee but for pipe commands instead of files. The Go implementation must match the\n  Homebrew reference binary (pee, installed by moreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by\n  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Read stdin and pipe it to multiple commands simultaneously.\n  - G2: Verify functional parity against the reference pee binary via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Pipe teeing\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must accept one or more COMMAND arguments. Must read stdin and write the input to the stdin of each COMMAND in parallel. Each COMMAND is executed via the shell (sh -c COMMAND).\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must wait for all commands to complete before exiting.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Stdout of each COMMAND goes to stdout, interleaved.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all commands exit 0. Must exit 1 when any command exits non-zero.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/pee does not implement output ordering or serialization of command outputs.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"echo hello | pee 'cat' 'wc -c' writes hello and byte count, matching reference.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"Differential test against reference pee passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"cmd/pee compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":58,"startLine":1,"totalLines":58}}}
