{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler-scaffold orchestrator) has assigned task #5633: implement `cmd/pee/main.go` for the `pee` moreutils utility. The task scope covers srd113-pee requirements R1.1, R1.2, and R1.3. pee reads stdin and writes it to the stdin of multiple shell commands simultaneously, with their stdout going to the process's stdout (interleaved). The implementation must follow the project's execution constitution, go style guide, and shared protocols. No git commands should be run; git is managed externally.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - `pee` is a moreutils utility that tees stdin to multiple pipe commands (like `tee` but for commands instead of files)\n   - Each COMMAND argument is executed via `sh -c COMMAND`\n   - Stdin must be read once and fanned out to all commands in parallel\n   - Commands' stdout goes to process stdout, interleaved (no ordering guarantees)\n   - Must wait for all commands to complete before exiting\n   - Exit 0 when all commands succeed, exit 1 when any fails (R2.1)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` (R2.2 / design decision D1)\n   - Differential testing pattern against reference `pee` binary from Homebrew moreutils\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` for test verification\n   - Copyright header: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd113-pee.yaml` (READ)\n     - Defines the full SRD for pee with requirements R1 (Pipe teeing) and R2 (Exit codes and SIGPIPE)\n     - R1.1: Accept COMMAND args, read stdin, write to each command's stdin in parallel via `sh -c`\n     - R1.2: Wait for all commands to complete before exiting\n     - R1.3: Stdout of each COMMAND goes to stdout, interleaved\n     - R2.1: Exit 0 when all succeed, exit 1 when any fails\n     - R2.2: Handle SIGPIPE via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler`\n     - non_goals: No output ordering or serialization\n     - package_contract imports: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n\n   - `docs/specs/use-cases/rel14.0-uc002-pee.yaml` (READ)\n     - Defines the use case: operator runs Go pee binary, differential test compares against reference\n     - Touchpoints: cmd/pee, pkg/testutils, pkg/sys\n\n   - `cmd/pee/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - The main implementation file for the pee utility\n     - Not yet created\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (PROVIDED IN CONTEXT)\n     - Contains `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` which must be called at start of main\n     ```go\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() {\n             <-c\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }()\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (PROVIDED IN CONTEXT)\n     - Contains `RunDiffTests`, `DiffTest`, `BuildBinary` for differential testing pattern\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The task had only just begun (two file reads completed) before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD and use case to understand exact requirements before implementation\n   - Identified the scope: task covers R1.1, R1.2, R1.3 (pipe teeing), plus D1 requires SIGPIPE handling\n   - No implementation has been written yet\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task description including role definition, repository structure, project context (vision, architecture, specs, roadmap, source code for all pkg/ files), requirement states, execution constitution, go style constitution, task details, constraints, and acceptance criteria. The