ors.AsType` for type-safe error handling\n- Command-line argument parsing without the `flag` package\n\n### Code Style Patterns\n\nBoth files follow these consistent patterns:\n1. **Copyright header:** `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` followed by `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n2. **Package comment:** Describes what the command implements and references spec numbers\n3. **SIGPIPE handling:** Both call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` as first thing in main\n4. **Exit pattern:** `os.Exit(run())` where run returns an int exit code\n5. **Error handling:** Wrapped with `fmt.Errorf()` using `%w` for error chain context\n6. **Local package imports:** All use `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n\nThese serve as excellent templates for implementing a similar `pee` utility following the established patterns in your codebase."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eda0914b-c5d5-43fb-b2bd-a6e814808fd4","uuid":"0c956403-42d4-49a6-862b-079b72855f5d","timestamp":"2026-05-28T17:05:32.795Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5633, find a cmd/ implementation that is similar in nature to pee (a moreutils utility that pipes stdin to multiple commands). Look for a simple moreutils utility like `sponge`, `ts`, `vidir`, `combine`, or `chronic` that has a main.go. Read one that exists and show me the full contents so I can see the code style, imports, copyright header, and patterns used. Also check the go.mod for the module path.","agentId":"a4d2250282009393e","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! I have both implementations. Let me provide you with a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Summary\n\nI found two excellent moreutils utility implementations in your codebase. Here are the details:\n\n### Module Path\n\nThe go.mod shows the module path is: **`github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`**\n\n### Sponge Implementation\n**